That error is almost certainly coming from a Supabase .single() query.

Meaning: the report-opening page expected exactly one matching report, but Supabase found either:

zero reports, usually because the email link is old/broken, or

multiple reports, usually because it is searching by car/date/circuit instead of the unique check_id.

That is why only some emails get it.

The proper fix is: email links must open reports by check_id, not by car/date/circuit, and any report fetch should use .maybeSingle() or .limit(1) instead of plain .single() unless the query is guaranteed unique.

